UID:state-corp-oklahoma-2025-05-15@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250516
SUMMARY:Oklahoma: State corporate income/franchise tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Form 512 due 30 days after the federal return's due date (~May 
 15). Extension mechanism confirmed directly: if no Oklahoma liability is ow
 ed\, an approved federal extension automatically extends the OK due date to
  match\; otherwise Form 504-C grants an extension not exceeding 7 months to
 tal. No single fixed calendar date is stated by Oklahoma's own instructions
  - it's a floating mechanism\, not a flat date\, confirmed directly against
  the 512-Pkt and 504-C instructions. | Form 512 due 30 days after the feder
 al return's due date (~May 15). Extension mechanism confirmed directly: if 
 no Oklahoma liability is owed\, an approved federal extension automatically
  extends the OK due date to match\; otherwise Form 504-C grants an extensio
 n not exceeding 7 months total. No single fixed calendar date is stated by 
 Oklahoma's own instructions - it's a floating mechanism\, not a flat date\,
  confirmed directly against the 512-Pkt and 504-C instructions. | Authority
 : Direct fetch of Oklahoma's 512-Pkt and Form 504-C instructions this sessi
 on: "Your Oklahoma return is due 30 days after the due date of your federal
  return." "An approved federal filing extension automatically extends the d
 ue date for your Oklahoma return" (if no OK liability owed)\; 504-C: "an ex
 tension may not exceed a total of 7 months." | Source: https://www.oklahoma
 .gov/content/dam/ok/en/tax/documents/forms/businesses/corporate-income-tax/
 current/512-Pkt.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may 
 not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source bef
 ore relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
